
These features could be done (but are currently not implemented):
-----------------------------------------------------------------

    XLib GUI surfaces:
        http://www.cairographics.org/manual/cairo-xlib-surface.html

    Quartz GUI surfaces:
        http://www.cairographics.org/manual/cairo-quartz-surface.html

    Win32 GUI surfaces:
        http://www.cairographics.org/manual/cairo-win32-surface.html

    PostScript surfaces:
        http://www.cairographics.org/manual/cairo-ps-surface.html
        
    Win32 fonts:
        http://www.cairographics.org/manual/cairo-win32-font.html
        
    Quartz fonts:
        http://www.cairographics.org/manual/cairo-quartz-font.html
        
    User fonts:
        http://www.cairographics.org/manual/cairo-user-font.html
        
    FreeType fonts:
        http://www.cairographics.org/manual/cairo-ft-font.html
        
    Font options:
        http://www.cairographics.org/manual/cairo-font-options.html
    

    cairo_surface_create_similar()
    
    cairo_surface_get_content ()

    cairo_surface_set_device_offset ()
    cairo_surface_get_device_offset ()

    cairo_surface_set_fallback_resolution ()
    cairo_surface_get_fallback_resolution ()
        - make these only for PDF surface (and other vector surfaces)
        
    cairo_get_target()
        - if this is implemented, it must be using the Lua objects and
        not the C++ Cairo API. Tie the original surface object to the
        context i.e. via registry, or environments.

    cairo_pop_group()
        - Is this needed; it returns the group as a pattern; is 'cairo_pop_group_to_source()' enough?

    cairo_get_group_target()
    
    cairo_pattern_get_surface()
        - if implemented, must return the Lua surface object used in creation of the pattern    
    
    cairo_show_text_glyphs()
    
    cairo_scaled_font_create()
    cairo_scaled_font_glyph_extents()
    
    cairo_scaled_font_text_to_glyphs()
    
    cairo_scaled_font_get_font_face()
    cairo_scaled_font_get_font_options()
    cairo_scaled_font_get_font_matrix()
    cairo_scaled_font_get_ctm()
    cairo_scaled_font_get_scale_matrix()
    cairo_scaled_font_get_type()

    cairo_toy_font_face_create()
    cairo_toy_font_face_get_family()
    cairo_toy_font_face_get_slant()
    cairo_toy_font_face_get_weight()
    
    Glyph stuff


These features are implemented using non-standard API approach:
---------------------------------------------------------------

    cairo_surface_get_content()     --> 'surf.info.content_*'
    cairo_surface_get_type()        --> 'surf.info.type'
    cairo_surface_has_show_text_glyphs()    --> 'surf.info.has_show_text_glyphs'

    cairo_get_*()           --> 'cr.info.*'


These features are skipped as unnecessary for scripting:
--------------------------------------------------------

    Image surface with pregiven bitmap contents:
        cairo_format_stride_for_width()
        cairo_image_surface_create_for_data()
        cairo_image_surface_get_data()
        cairo_image_surface_get_stride()
        cairo_image_surface_create_from_png_stream()

    These are not needed by script level:
        *_reference()
        *_destroy()
        *_status()
        *_reference_count()
        *_user_data()

    cairo_surface_mark_dirty ()
    cairo_surface_mark_dirty_rectangle ()
    
    cairo_get_dash_count()
    cairo_get_color_stop_count()
        - used for allocating enough buffer; not needed in scripts



(end)
